I1017 09:09:41.171969    7700 input_loop.go:106] HandleUserInput called with text: "The Worker has stopped in step 1 (stopped for approval). This run is condition F: there are no issue files. The Worker's latest chat reply is pasted below between the markers. You may also read the code and data in the Worker workspace (read-only). Then show your review (Part 1) and your draft to the Worker (Part 2) in full in your reply, in the format of Section 4 of MANAGER_BRIEF.md (in condition F, every draft is a chat message), and append \"Manager memo 01\" to memos/thm01-R-gemini38f-r2-F/manager_memo.md as in Section 5. Append only: do not modify or delete any existing text in the memo file. Do not edit any other file.\n\n----- WORKER REPLY (pasted by the human) -----\n### C(n+1) Basis, Root System, and PBW Ordering Design (Issue I01-1)\n\n---\n\n### 1. Notation Conventions for Generators & Oscillators\n\n#### Oscillators\n- **Fermionic standard pair** ($p=1$):\n  - $a_1^+$ (`a_1_p`), $a_1^-$ (`a_1_m`) with CAR: $\\{a_1^-, a_1^+\\} = 1$, $(a_1^\\pm)^2 = 0$.\n- **Bosonic oscillators** ($p=0$):\n  - $b_k^+$ (`b_k_p`), $b_k^-$ (`b_k_m`) for $k = 1, \\dots, n$ with CCR: $[b_j^-, b_k^+] = \\delta_{jk}$.\n- **Central elements**:\n  - $K$: Central scalar ($K = 1$).\n  - $\\kappa$: Odd central nilpotent parameter ($p(\\kappa) = 1$, $\\kappa^2 = 0$).\n\n#### Generator Labels and Realizations\n| Category | Generator Label | Root | Realization in Oscillators | Parity |\n|---|---|---|---|:---:|\n| **Cartan** | `H_1` | — | $a_1^+ a_1^- + b_1^+ b_1^-$ | 0 |\n| | `H_k` ($2 \\leq k \\leq n$) | — | $b_{k-1}^+ b_{k-1}^- - b_k^+ b_k^-$ | 0 |\n| | `H_{n+1}` | — | $-b_n^+ b_n^- - \\tfrac{1}{2}$ | 0 |\n| **Long Even Roots** | `E_2del{k}_p` | $+2\\delta_k$ | $(b_k^+)^2$ | 0 |\n| | `E_2del{k}_m` | $-2\\delta_k$ | $(b_k^-)^2$ | 0 |\n| **Short Even Roots** ($i < j$) | `E_del{i}_del{j}_pp` | $+\\delta_i + \\delta_j$ | $b_i^+ b_j^+$ | 0 |\n| | `E_del{i}_del{j}_pm` | $+\\delta_i - \\delta_j$ | $b_i^+ b_j^-$ | 0 |\n| | `E_del{i}_del{j}_mp` | $-\\delta_i + \\delta_j$ | $b_i^- b_j^+$ | 0 |\n| | `E_del{i}_del{j}_mm` | $-\\delta_i - \\delta_j$ | $b_i^- b_j^-$ | 0 |\n| **Odd Roots** ($1 \\leq k \\leq n$) | `E_eps1_del{k}_pp` | $+\\varepsilon + \\delta_k$ | $a_1^+ b_k^+$ | 1 |\n| | `E_eps1_del{k}_pm` | $+\\varepsilon - \\delta_k$ | $a_1^+ b_k^-$ | 1 |\n| | `E_eps1_del{k}_mp` | $-\\varepsilon + \\delta_k$ | $a_1^- b_k^+$ | 1 |\n| | `E_eps1_del{k}_mm` | $-\\varepsilon - \\delta_k$ | $a_1^- b_k^-$ | 1 |\n\n---\n\n### 2. Basis Lists for $C(2)$, $C(3)$, and $C(4)$\n\nDimension formula: $\\dim(C(n+1)) = (2n^2 + n + 1) \\mid 4n$.\n\n#### $C(2) = \\mathfrak{osp}(2|2)$ ($n=1$): $\\dim = 4 \\mid 4$, Total = 8\n- **Even Basis** (4):\n  `[\"H_1\", \"H_2\", \"E_2del1_p\", \"E_2del1_m\"]`\n- **Odd Basis** (4):\n  `[\"E_eps1_del1_pp\", \"E_eps1_del1_pm\", \"E_eps1_del1_mp\", \"E_eps1_del1_mm\"]`\n\n#### $C(3) = \\mathfrak{osp}(2|4)$ ($n=2$): $\\dim = 11 \\mid 8$, Total = 19\n- **Even Basis** (11):\n  - Cartan (3): `[\"H_1\", \"H_2\", \"H_3\"]`\n  - Long roots (4): `[\"E_2del1_p\", \"E_2del2_p\", \"E_2del1_m\", \"E_2del2_m\"]`\n  - Short roots (4): `[\"E_del1_del2_pp\", \"E_del1_del2_mm\", \"E_del1_del2_pm\", \"E_del1_del2_mp\"]`\n- **Odd Basis** (8):\n  - $k=1$: `[\"E_eps1_del1_pp\", \"E_eps1_del1_pm\", \"E_eps1_del1_mp\", \"E_eps1_del1_mm\"]`\n  - $k=2$: `[\"E_eps1_del2_pp\", \"E_eps1_del2_pm\", \"E_eps1_del2_mp\", \"E_eps1_del2_mm\"]`\n\n#### $C(4) = \\mathfrak{osp}(2|6)$ ($n=3$): $\\dim = 22 \\mid 12$, Total = 34\n- **Even Basis** (22):\n  - Cartan (4): `[\"H_1\", \"H_2\", \"H_3\", \"H_4\"]`\n  - Long roots (6): `[\"E_2del1_p\", \"E_2del2_p\", \"E_2del3_p\", \"E_2del1_m\", \"E_2del2_m\", \"E_2del3_m\"]`\n  - Short roots (12):\n    - pair (1,2): `[\"E_del1_del2_pp\", \"E_del1_del2_mm\", \"E_del1_del2_pm\", \"E_del1_del2_mp\"]`\n    - pair (1,3): `[\"E_del1_del3_pp\", \"E_del1_del3_mm\", \"E_del1_del3_pm\", \"E_del1_del3_mp\"]`\n    - pair (2,3): `[\"E_del2_del3_pp\", \"E_del2_del3_mm\", \"E_del2_del3_pm\", \"E_del2_del3_mp\"]`\n- **Odd Basis** (12):\n  - $k=1$: `[\"E_eps1_del1_pp\", \"E_eps1_del1_pm\", \"E_eps1_del1_mp\", \"E_eps1_del1_mm\"]`\n  - $k=2$: `[\"E_eps1_del2_pp\", \"E_eps1_del2_pm\", \"E_eps1_del2_mp\", \"E_eps1_del2_mm\"]`\n  - $k=3$: `[\"E_eps1_del3_pp\", \"E_eps1_del3_pm\", \"E_eps1_del3_mp\", \"E_eps1_del3_mm\"]`\n\n---\n\n### 3. Concrete PBW Ordering Options for Selection\n\nIn all options, the global graded ordering follows the base convention:\n$$\\kappa < [\\text{odd basis}] < [\\text{even basis}]$$\n\nWe propose two concrete ordering schemes for the internal arrangement of the odd basis:\n\n#### Option A: Bosonic Mode Block Ordering (Recommended)\n- **Structure**: Group primarily by the bosonic oscillator index $k \\in \\{1, \\dots, n\\}$, and secondarily by the signs of $\\varepsilon$ and $\\delta_k$ (`pp`, `pm`, `mp`, `mm`).\n- **Order for $n=2$**:\n  `E_eps1_del1_pp`, `E_eps1_del1_pm`, `E_eps1_del1_mp`, `E_eps1_del1_mm`,\n  `E_eps1_del2_pp`, `E_eps1_del2_pm`, `E_eps1_del2_mp`, `E_eps1_del2_mm`\n- **Rationale**: Directly aligns with the $4 \\times 1$ block structure of the deformation matrix $\\mathrm{gb}_{\\sigma, j, s}$ for each bosonic mode $j$. Simplifies indexing, tensor blocks, and coboundary matrix representations.\n\n#### Option B: Global Root Polarity Split (Direct $B(0,n)$ Analogue)\n- **Structure**: Group all positive $\\varepsilon$ roots first, then all negative $\\varepsilon$ roots, matching the positive-then-negative convention of $B(0,n)$ (where all `E_del{k}_p` precede all `E_del{k}_m`).\n- **Order for $n=2$**:\n  - Positive $\\varepsilon$:\n    `E_eps1_del1_pp`, `E_eps1_del2_pp`, `E_eps1_del1_pm`, `E_eps1_del2_pm`\n  - Negative $\\varepsilon$:\n    `E_eps1_del1_mp`, `E_eps1_del2_mp`, `E_eps1_del1_mm`, `E_eps1_del2_mm`\n- **Rationale**: Strictly preserves the root polarity partitioning $\\Delta_{\\bar{1}}^+ < \\Delta_{\\bar{1}}^-$.\n\n---\n\n### Human Approval Required\nPlease confirm whether you prefer **Option A (Mode Block)** or **Option B (Polarity Split)**, or specify any adjustment to the conventions. No files will be modified until your approval is received.\n----- END OF WORKER REPLY -----"
